# {{lb|en|idiomatic|informal}} [[available|Available]] for [[anyone]] to [[obtain]], [[claim]], [[decide]], or [[win]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 13 1998|author=w:Salman Rushdie|title=Mohandas Gandhi|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120516230218/http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,988159,00.html|journal=Time
|passage=Gandhi today is '''up for grabs'''. He has become abstract, ahistorical, postmodern, no longer a man in and of his time but a freeloading concept.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Nov 5 2006|author=[[w:Robert Hicks (American author)|Robert Hicks]]|title=Opinion: Separate but Equal|titleurl=http://www.nytimes.com/2006/11/05/opinion/05hicks.html|journal=New York Times|accessdate=12 July 2011
|passage=The Senate is '''up for grabs''' in November's election.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Nov 18 2009|author=Julie Schmit|title=China pushes solar, wind power development|titleurl=http://www.usatoday.com/tech/news/2009-11-17-chinasolar17_CV_N.htm|journal=USA Today|accessdate=12 July 2011
|passage="In the transformation of clean technology, it's '''up for grabs''' whether the giants will be American or Chinese or from other countries," says Salzman.}}

